$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Which of the following ordered pairs <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_006_7284e904.png" alt="x comma y "></span></span> is a solution to the system of inequalities above?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_000_8deb0015.png\" alt=\"1 comma 0\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_001_81500b57.png\" alt=\"negative 1 comma 0\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_002_c9aac4fe.png\" alt=\"0 comma 1\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_003_5ac4a519.png\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The solutions to the given system of inequalities is the set of all ordered pairs <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_007_f2fea45d.png" alt="x comma y "></span> that satisfy both inequalities in the system. For an ordered pair to satisfy the inequality <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_008_2d164414.png" alt="y is less than or equal to x"></span>, the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class="italic">y</span>-coordinate must be less than or equal to the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate. This is true of the ordered pair <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_009_5ac4a519.png" alt="0 comma negative 1"></span>, because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_010_e5325e88.png" alt="negative 1 is less than or equal to 0"></span>. To satisfy the inequality <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_011_b6f7b5da.png" alt="y is less than or equal to negative x"></span>, the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class="italic">y</span>-coordinate must be less than or equal to the value of the additive inverse of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate. This is also true of the ordered pair <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_012_5ac4a519.png" alt="0 comma negative 1"></span>. Because 0 is its own additive inverse, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_013_a6b63e64.png" alt="negative 1 is less than or equal to the negative of 0"></span>&nbsp;is the same as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_014_e5325e88.png" alt="negative 1 is less than or equal to 0"></span>. Therefore, the ordered pair <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_015_5ac4a519.png" alt="0 comma negative 1"></span> is a solution to the given system of inequalities.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies only the inequality <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_016_2d164414.png" alt="y is less than or equal to x"></span> in the given system, not both inequalities. Choice B incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies only the inequality <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_017_b6f7b5da.png" alt="y is less than or equal to negative x"></span> in the system, but not both inequalities. Choice C is incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies neither inequality.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 18, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"968e9e51","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"032729-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.E.","skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_004_2d164414.png\" alt=\"Inequality 1: y is less than or equal to x.\"></span></span></p><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_005_b6f7b5da.png\" alt=\"Inequality 2: y is less than or equal to negative x.\"></span></span></p></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following ordered pairs <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_006_7284e904.png\" alt=\"x comma y \"></span></span> is a solution to the system of inequalities above?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_000_8deb0015.png\" alt=\"1 comma 0\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_001_81500b57.png\" alt=\"negative 1 comma 0\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_002_c9aac4fe.png\" alt=\"0 comma 1\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_003_5ac4a519.png\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The solutions to the given system of inequalities is the set of all ordered pairs <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_007_f2fea45d.png\" alt=\"x comma y \"></span> that satisfy both inequalities in the system. For an ordered pair to satisfy the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_008_2d164414.png\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to x\"></span>, the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate must be less than or equal to the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-coordinate. This is true of the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_009_5ac4a519.png\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span>, because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_010_e5325e88.png\" alt=\"negative 1 is less than or equal to 0\"></span>. To satisfy the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_011_b6f7b5da.png\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to negative x\"></span>, the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate must be less than or equal to the value of the additive inverse of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-coordinate. This is also true of the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_012_5ac4a519.png\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span>. Because 0 is its own additive inverse, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_013_a6b63e64.png\" alt=\"negative 1 is less than or equal to the negative of 0\"></span>&nbsp;is the same as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_014_e5325e88.png\" alt=\"negative 1 is less than or equal to 0\"></span>. Therefore, the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_015_5ac4a519.png\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span> is a solution to the given system of inequalities.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies only the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_016_2d164414.png\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to x\"></span> in the given system, not both inequalities. Choice B incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies only the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/968e9e51/img_017_b6f7b5da.png\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to negative x\"></span> in the system, but not both inequalities. Choice C is incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies neither inequality.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":18,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959627,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"968e9e51","skill_cd":"H.E.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","createDate":1691007959627,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"032729-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"351701f2-411f-43ef-8680-fba54dbbe043","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"032729-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Inequality 1: y is less than or equal to x.\"></span></span></p><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Inequality 2: y is less than or equal to negative x.\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following ordered pairs <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x comma y \"></span></span> is a solution to the system of inequalities above?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 comma 0\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 1 comma 0\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 comma 1\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The solutions to the given system of inequalities is the set of all ordered pairs <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x comma y \"></span> that satisfy both inequalities in the system. For an ordered pair to satisfy the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to x\"></span>, the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate must be less than or equal to the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-coordinate. This is true of the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span>, because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 1 is less than or equal to 0\"></span>. To satisfy the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to negative x\"></span>, the value of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate must be less than or equal to the value of the additive inverse of the ordered pair&rsquo;s <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-coordinate. This is also true of the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span>. Because 0 is its own additive inverse, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 1 is less than or equal to the negative of 0\"></span>&nbsp;is the same as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 1 is less than or equal to 0\"></span>. Therefore, the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 comma negative 1\"></span> is a solution to the given system of inequalities.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies only the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to x\"></span> in the given system, not both inequalities. Choice B incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies only the inequality <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y is less than or equal to negative x\"></span> in the system, but not both inequalities. Choice C is incorrect. This ordered pair satisfies neither inequality.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959627,"updateDate":1691007959627}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959627, 1691007959627),
