ght parenthesis equals x minus 39\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>39</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"ee5a89f5-3021-4f8a-8a99-6b9c30551500","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 39 x\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>39</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"}],"keys":["ee5a89f5-3021-4f8a-8a99-6b9c30551500"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. An equation defining a linear function can be written in the form <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> is the slope and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma b right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. It&rsquo;s given that the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> has a slope of <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math>, so <math alttext=\"m equals 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, so <math alttext=\"b equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</ma