</mfrac>
</mrow>
<mo>+</mo>
<mfrac>
<mn>5</mn>
<mn>6</mn>
</mfrac>
</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the point <math alttext="left parenthesis r comma minus StartFraction 7 r Over 6 EndFraction plus five sixths right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, not the point <math alttext="left parenthesis r comma StartFraction 7 r Over 6 EndFraction plus five sixths right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, lies on the graph of each equation.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. Substituting <math alttext="StartFraction r Over 4 EndFraction plus 5"><mrow>
