6.png" alt="l"></span> has a slope of 0.<p>Choice B is incorrect. A line with slope&nbsp;<span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/98d3393a/img_009_cf8b7131.png" alt="negative one half"></span> is perpendicular to a line with slope 2. However, the line with equation <span class="italic">x</span> = 2 is vertical and has undefined slope (not slope of 2).&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. A line with slope &ndash;2 is perpendicular to a line with slope <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/98d3393a/img_010_6b62f681.png" alt="one half"></span>. However, the line with equation<span class="italic"> x</span> = 2 has undefined slope (not slope of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/98d3393a/img_011_6b62f681.png" alt="one half"></span>). Choice D is incorrect; this is the slope of the line <span class="italic">x</span> = 2 itself, not the slope of a line perpendicular to it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
