>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis negative five thirds right parenthesis left parenthesis negative 6 right parenthesis plus b\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, which is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"0 equals 10 plus b\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"negative 10 equals b\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of line <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative 10\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the <em>xy</em>-plane, line <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> has a slope of <math alttext=\"negative five thirds\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math> and an <em>x</em>-intercept of <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 6 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. What is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of line <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>?</p>","type":"spr","correct_answer":["-10"]},"createDate":1730147357391,"updateDate":1730147357391}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357391, 1730147357391),
