<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a line" class="sr-only"><ul><li>The line slants gradually down from left to right.</li>
<li>The line passes through the following points:<br>
<ul>
<li>(8 comma 10)</li>
<li>(9 comma 9)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane models the possible combinations of length <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="in meters left parenthesis m right parenthesis"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mtext>m</mtext><mo>)</mo></math>, and width <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, in meters, for a rectangle with a perimeter of <math alttext="36 m"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"dce267f2-b304-45b1-9180-f66444d848ba","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter, and the width is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter.</p>"},{"id":"9c378fb6-f446-4391-a299-5e1027de2e92","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>, and the width is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"94896bc1-a01f-44d3-9500-38285d22eabf","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>, and the width is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"0fd2fb98-8f33-4a95-b0ec-38ee185a7e6b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter, and the width is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["94896bc1-a01f-44d3-9500-38285d22eabf"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It’s given that the graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane models the possible combinations of length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math>, in meters (m), and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>, in meters, for a rectangle with a perimeter of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="36"><mn>36</mn></math> m. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> represents the length, in meters, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> represents the width, in meters, the point <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;in the <em>xy</em>-plane represents a rectangle whose length is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> m and whose width is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> m.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
