xt=\"in meters left parenthesis m right parenthesis\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mtext>m</mtext><mo>)</mo></math>, and width <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, in meters, for a rectangle with a perimeter of <math alttext=\"36 m\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"dce267f2-b304-45b1-9180-f66444d848ba","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter, and the width is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter.</p>"},{"id":"9c378fb6-f446-4391-a299-5e1027de2e92","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>, and the width is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"94896bc1-a01f-44d3-9500-38285d22eabf","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>, and the width is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"0fd2fb98-8f33-4a95-b0ec-38ee185a7e6b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter, and the width is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter.</p>"}],"keys":["94896bc1-a01f-44d3-9500-38285d22eabf"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It’s given that the graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane models the possible combinations of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, in meters (m), and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, in meters, for a rectangle with a perimeter of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> m. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> represents the length, in meters, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> represents the width, in meters, the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;in the <em>xy</em>-plane represents a rectangle whose length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> m and whose width is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> m.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is an interpretation of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 10 comma 8 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017718,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"9b0a4eae","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1755117017718,"program":"SAT","primary_c