\n      <use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <defs>\n     <path d=\"M 0 3 \nC 0.795609 3 1.55874 2.683901 2.12132 2.12132 \nC 2.683901 1.55874 3 0.795609 3 0 \nC 3 -0.795609 2.683901 -1.55874 2.12132 -2.12132 \nC 1.55874 -2.683901 0.795609 -3 0 -3 \nC -0.795609 -3 -1.55874 -2.683901 -2.12132 -2.12132 \nC -2.683901 -1.55874 -3 -0.795609 -3 0 \nC -3 0.795609 -2.683901 1.55874 -2.12132 2.12132 \nC -1.55874 2.683901 -0.795609 3 0 3 \nz\n\" id=\"m977a4c3e08\" style=\"stroke:#000000;\"></path>\n    </defs>\n    <g clip-path=\"url(#p02cea6bb41)\">\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"122.750292\" xlink:href=\"#m977a4c3e08\" y=\"140.390597\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p02cea6bb41)\" d=\"M 41.860197 59.500502 \nL 223.86291 241.503216 \nL 223.86291 241.503216 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p02cea6bb41\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"262.488358\" x=\"9.200821\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a line\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The line slants gradually down from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(8 comma 10)</li>\n<li>(9 comma 9)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane models the possible combinations of length <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"in meters left parenthesis m right parenthesis\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mtext>m</mtext><mo>)</mo></math>, and width <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, in meters, for a rectangle with a perimeter of <math alttext=\"36 m\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>","keys":["94896bc1-a01f-44d3-9500-38285d22eabf"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"dce267f2-b304-45b1-9180-f66444d848ba","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter, and the width is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter.</p>"},{"id":"9c378fb6-f446-4391-a299-5e1027de2e92","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>, and the width is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"94896bc1-a01f-44d3-9500-38285d22eabf","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>, and the width is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"0fd2fb98-8f33-4a95-b0ec-38ee185a7e6b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length is <math alttext=\"8 m\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter, and the width is <math alttext=\"10 m\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> less than the perimeter.</p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It’s given that the graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane models the possible combinations of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, in meters (m), and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, in meters, for a rectangle with a perimeter of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> m. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> represents the length, in meters, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> represents the width, in meters, the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;in the <em>xy</em>-plane represents a rectangle whose length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> m and whose width is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> m.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is an interpretation of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 10 comma 8 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 10 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","externalid":"4d7cd4c5-d45b-40fb-8391-76021972ba43","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1755117017718,"updateDate":1755117017718}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017718, 1755117017718),
    ($SATQ$9b886541$SATQ$, $SATQ$8076db82-ac6c-4ac2-a6b7-46a9a4b4059b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in one variable$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">If <math alttext="3 x minus 8 equals 7"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>3</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>8</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, what is the value of <math alttext="3 x plus 8"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>3</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>8</mn>
</mrow>
</math>?</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"67cd1793-b2cb-45e1-abfb-e977ee772801","content":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><math alttext=\"negative 1\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn>\n</math></span></p>"},{"id":"10fbb038-b7ae-4e37-ba59-d089c4f3febe","content":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></span></p>"},{"id":"fd5d12b1-6639-49d8-b152-1898ce16266f","content":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></span></p>"},{"id":"e80968e7-9cde-4ed1-aa26-c2fe52516c0b","content":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></span></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e80968e7-9cde-4ed1-aa26-c2fe52516c0b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. It's given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x minus 8 equals 7"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. Adding&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> to both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x equals 15"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>. Adding <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> to both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x plus 8 equals 23"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x plus 8"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="23"><mn>23</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x plus 8"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>
